**No, I am 0% sure. There are 48 defensive programming patterns (`|| 0`, `|| 1`, `|| 0.X`) remaining in effectsEngine.ts that need to be fixed.**

These patterns violate the no-defensive-programming principle established in CLAUDE.md (lines 598-653). Each one should be replaced with explicit initialization checks like:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Current code
const value = (gameState.foo as any).bar || 0.5;

