   - Zero overhead in production
   - Comprehensive coverage during testing

**Benefits Demonstrated**:
- Proxy caught NaN/Infinity writes automatically
- Manual assertions provide detailed context
- Production performance unaffected
- Best of both worlds

### Problem: How to Prevent NaN Propagation
**Solution**: ES6 Proxy intercepts all property writes and validates numeric values
**Pattern**:
```typescript
set(obj, prop, value, receiver) {
  if (typeof value === 'number' && !isFinite(value)) {
    throw createValidationError([...path, propKey], value, 'write');
  }
  return Reflect.set(obj, prop, value, receiver);
}
```

### Problem: How to Avoid Infinite Recursion in Proxy
**Solution**: WeakMap cache
```typescript
const proxyCache = new WeakMap<object, any>();

if (proxyCache.has(target)) {
  return proxyCache.get(target);
}
const proxy = new Proxy(target, { ... });
proxyCache.set(target, proxy);
